 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Trading transactions are the purchase and sale of goods.\nDocuments:\n• the purchase order (bon de commande): the buyer asks for goods;\n• the delivery note (bon de livraison): sent with the goods; the buyer checks and signs it;\n• the invoice (facture): states the goods, quantities, prices, discounts, VAT and the amount to pay — the main document for recording;\n• the credit note (avoir): reduces an invoice (goods returned, extra discount);\n• the receipt (reçu): proof that payment was made.\nInventory: counting and valuing the goods in stock, at least once a year at the end of the year. Stock at the end = stock at the start + purchases − goods sold.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "s": 200,
   "b": 450,
   "x": 380
  },
  "problem": "A shop starts with {s} bags of rice, buys {b} and sells {x}. How many bags are in stock at the end?",
  "steps": [
   "End stock = start stock + purchases − sales.",
   "{s} + {b} − {x} = {s + b - x} bags."
  ],
  "answer": "{s + b - x} bags",
  "checks": []
 },
